          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em cohomology operation
            is a family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            between
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
            with respect to the base space.
          %p
            Equivalently, if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            (as it does for all usual notions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theories"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps between classifying spaces.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
