                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi X
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cup^E_X
              is the operation of forming the
              %a{:href => "cup+product#CupProductInWhiteheadGeneralizedCohomologyTheory"} E-cup product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of its elements.
            %p
              Both of these operations are clearly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              (for the first this is evident, for the second this comes down to the fact that the
              %a{:href => "suspension+spectrum#SmashMonoidalDiagonals"} smash-monoidal diagonals of suspension spectra
              are natural, hence are indeed
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category+with+diagonals"} monoidal diagonals
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} fully-faithfulness
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi PointedTopologicalSpaces
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Functors
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi PointedTopologicalSpaces
                    %msup
